  h1="Staying with a local during the Four Days Marches"
>
  <p>
    A room, garden, or driveway at someone's home — often more affordable than a hotel,
    more personal than a campsite, and a good alternative when the regular options are
    full.
  </p>

  <h2>What to expect</h2>
  <p>
    Ranges from a simple camping spot in a backyard to a full guest room. Facilities
    vary per host — ask in advance what is and isn't included (sanitary facilities,
    breakfast, parking).
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    Usually lower than a hotel, comparable to or cheaper than camping, depending on
    facilities.
  </p>

  <h2>What to pay attention to</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Distance to the start/route</li>
    <li>Exactly what's included</li>
    <li>Clear agreements on arrival and departure times</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Haven't found a place yet?</h2>
  <p>
    Also check <a href="/en/camping">camping</a> or
    <a href="/en/hotels-bb">hotels &amp; B&amp;Bs</a>.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
